1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,532
Your organisation wants to put AI to work.

2
00:00:03,647 --> 00:00:07,832
But the teams responsible for introducing it are already stretched.

3
00:00:07,947 --> 00:00:14,398
Are the right protections in place? Where should they start? And who needs to act?

4
00:00:14,513 --> 00:00:17,198
A readiness report can identify gaps.

5
00:00:17,313 --> 00:00:21,198
Turning those findings into progress is the next challenge.

6
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:26,632
Meet AI Flight Deck—an orchestration tool for Copilot readiness and rollout.

7
00:00:26,747 --> 00:00:35,032
Built for Microsoft 365 Copilot, it brings together three things: visibility, clear next actions, and evidence of progress.

8
00:00:35,567 --> 00:00:40,532
Connect your tenant, select your pilot group, and run read-only checks.

9
00:00:40,647 --> 00:00:44,065
Explore thirteen readiness domains, from SharePoint and OneDrive

10
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,432
to adoption, measurement, and governance,

11
00:00:46,547 --> 00:00:48,332
then identity and access.

12
00:00:48,447 --> 00:00:51,532
Here, an identity protection check needs attention.

13
00:00:51,647 --> 00:00:57,832
Instead of leaving the team with a finding, Flight Deck provides a path forward:

14
00:00:57,947 --> 00:00:59,732
record the responsible owner,

15
00:00:59,847 --> 00:01:01,198
follow the guidance,

16
00:01:01,313 --> 00:01:05,132
and make the change through the normal administration process.

17
00:01:05,247 --> 00:01:09,132
The work is marked complete. But did it work?

18
00:01:09,247 --> 00:01:11,998
A completed task is not proof.

19
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:13,632
Collect fresh evidence.

20
00:01:13,747 --> 00:01:16,932
This supported configuration check is now verified.

21
00:01:17,047 --> 00:01:18,865
Other gaps remain visible.

22
00:01:18,980 --> 00:01:25,598
The team can see what changed, what remains unresolved, and what needs a decision.

23
00:01:25,713 --> 00:01:31,998
When they check again, if the evidence no longer supports the result, the action reopens.

24
00:01:32,113 --> 00:01:35,932
For customers, a clearer path from uncertainty to action.

25
00:01:36,047 --> 00:01:42,165
For Microsoft and partners, a repeatable way to help customers address Copilot adoption blockers.

26
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:45,698
Start with a pilot. Repeat as rollout expands.

27
00:01:45,813 --> 00:01:47,165
AI Flight Deck.

28
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,498
Do not just assess readiness.

29
00:01:49,613 --> 00:01:53,865
Turn findings into a flight plan—and progress into evidence.
